(7259705, 1128509, 13077, '<td valign="top">This could have been a lot sharper if you had enough light to use a much faster shutter speed. It looks like it could have been a controlled environment. Usually when you are shooting a macro you want as much light as you can get, often you will need a flash or a continuos light or at a least a reflector to get light in the right places.</td>', 'This could have been a lot sharper if you had enough light to use a much faster shutter speed. It looks like it could have been a controlled environment. Usually when you are shooting a macro you want as much light as you can get, often you will need a flash or a continuos light or at a least a reflector to get light in the right places.', '2014-09-06 00:22:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(7259706, 1128487, 24983, '<td valign="top">maybe a plant of some type? darn it I will never know for sure</td>', 'maybe a plant of some type? darn it I will never know for sure', '2014-09-06 00:23:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(7259707, 1128506, 13077, '<td valign="top">I think the depth of field is too shallow, and there seems to be some motion blur so nothing in the photo seems sharp. Light is always your friend with macro, anything you can do to bring light onto the subject and increase the shutter speed will help when you are so close to the subject.</td>', 'I think the depth of field is too shallow, and there seems to be some motion blur so nothing in the photo seems sharp. Light is always your friend with macro, anything you can do to bring light onto the subject and increase the shutter speed will help when you are so close to the subject.', '2014-09-06 00:23:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(7259708, 1129029, 13077, '<td valign="top">The colors and composition look nice, but usually at least a little bit of in-focus area helps.</td>', 'The colors and composition look nice, but usually at least a little bit of in-focus area helps.', '2014-09-06 00:23:56.000000', NULL, 1),
